null,"main_deck":"[\"88264978\",\"25554552\",\"25554552\",\"68464358\",\"68464358\",\"68464358\",\"32476603\",\"67127799\",\"5969957\",\"5969957\",\"26655293\",\"67748760\",\"67748760\",\"98937206\",\"70333910\",\"48355999\",\"93969023\",\"93969023\",\"93969023\",\"14558127\",\"14558127\",\"14558127\",\"42141493\",\"42141493\",\"42141493\",\"94145021\",\"94145021\",\"31443476\",\"31443476\",\"31443476\",\"36668118\",\"6556178\",\"38129297\",\"46411259\",\"46411259\",\"46411259\",\"62265044\",\"54693926\",\"54693926\",\"54693926\",\"73628505\",\"18144507\",\"24224830\",\"65681983\",\"10045474\",\"10045474\",\"10045474\",\"87607094\"]","extra_deck":"[\"84464389\",\"37818794\",\"13756293\",\"5041348\",\"98630720\",\"66452432\",\"85289965\",\"3957130\",\"23732205\",\"90011273\",\"11969228\",\"65741787\",\"24361622\",\"13143275\",\"73539069\"]","side_deck":"[\"27204311\",\"27204311\",\"97268402\",\"97268402\",\"97268402\",\"73642297\",\"73642297\",\"73642297\",\"70538272\",\"44146295\",\"92892239\",\"69946549\",\"63519819\",\"29301450\",\"29296344\"]","edit_date":"1 hour ago","deck_views":1,"deckNum":737951,"comments":0,"cover_card":"84464389","deck_price":"81.04","pretty_url":"rokket-metamorphosis-737951","rating":null,"ratingq":null,"format":"Fun/Casual Decks","common":150,"rare":300,"super":630,"ultra":810,"img_url":"https://images.ygoprodeck.com/images/users/276576/276576_1760557775.jpg","submit_date":"1 hour ago","tournamentPlayerName":null,"tournamentName":null,"tournamentPlayerCount":null,"tournamentPlayerCountIsApproximate":null,"tournamentPlacement":null,"userid":276576},{"username":"Vsin","deck_name":"R.B.E.S. - Vancouver Regional, 14th out of 60 (4-2)","deck_description":"<p>Another \"I didn't actually top\" decklist, but I'm very happy with how the list performed so I wanted to do another writeup.</p><p>I was scared of Angelechy going into the regional, but then ran into two of them and just...walked straight through their endboard only mildly singed by Destrier, and ended up never needing to think about Shatranga. I wanted three Typhoons but only had one, so I chucked in two Cosmic Cyclone, actually saw the Cyclone, and then never had to use it.</p><p>Boss on Parade bridging into Crystron via Gray Layer is actually way better than I expected, because it means 11 out of ~17-18 + 3 Mammoth starters end in followup for next turn. And that kept coming up every single round. I only mained 2 Funk Dock because even though it's the best starter going 1st, it's awful to see in your opening hand going 2nd.</p><p>Mammoth paired with Metal Slave is a surprisingly good boardbreaker that goes 2-for-1 at minimum, but I only ever saw Mammoth going 1st and only I resolved the Helping Robo search once. I don't agree with trying to Clockwork Night for it, Helping Robo gets locked out if you resolve Cannon and summon a non-machine from your opponent's hand.</p><p>----</p><p>Matchups: Rolad Branded (lost die / LL), VSK9 (won die / WW), Angelechy (lost die / WW), Angelechy (won die / WW), Rolad 60card (won die / LWL), Yummy Azamina FTK (won die / WLW).</p><p>Both losses make the Rolad matchup look bad, but R1 G1 I opened double nib into &lt; 5 summons and got drolled, G2 no starters in a deck that should have ~95% consistency. R5 was G1 Fuwa + handtraps + Goemon (I skipped Cannon because Fuwa), G3 I opened no non-engine and scooped to avoid a double loss.</p>","deck_excerpt":"R.B. Crystron B.E.S.","youtube_link":null,"main_deck":"[\"44573911\",\"81794107\",\"79436874\",\"33438265\",\"6043161\",\"5109321\",\"5109321\",\"5109321\",\"78710386\",\"78710386\",\"79859067\",\"25865565\",\"83443619\",\"83443619\",\"83443619\",\"31552317\",\"31552317\",\"31552317\",\"81439174\",\"41516133\",\"84257883\",\"18616294\",\"4909946\",\"4909946\",\"4909946\",\"52340444\",\"3434362\",\"3434362\",\"3434362\",\"42141493\",\"42141493\",\"42141493\",\"84192580\",\"84192580\",\"14558127\",\"14558127\",\"14558127\",\"27204311\",\"27204311\",\"27204311\",\"9414502